---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site, SITE_URL, addressLines } from '../data/site';

/**
 * Content follows the supplied privacy-policy document. The only edit is
 * resolving "[Insert Website URL]" to SITE_URL, plus a cookies section that
 * matches what this site actually does: Google Analytics and the Meta Pixel.
 */
const host = SITE_URL.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  metaTitle={`Privacy policy — ${site.name}`}
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and safeguards your personal information.`}
  lead="How we collect, use, disclose and safeguard your data when you visit this site or engage our services."
  updated="18 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal
    information. This policy outlines how we handle your data when you visit
    <a href={SITE_URL}>{host}</a> or engage with our services.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Personal data</h3>
  <p>
    When you fill out a contact form, request a consultation or subscribe to our
    newsletter, we may collect personally identifiable information including your full
    name, email address, phone number, company name and website URL.
  </p>
  <h3>Technical and usage data</h3>
  <p>
    When you navigate our website, our servers may automatically collect information such
    as your IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URLs, page views, and
    the dates and times of your visits.
  </p>
  <h3>Marketing and campaign data</h3>
  <p>
    Information required to execute digital marketing campaigns on your behalf, which may
    include audience analytics, customer lists and advertising performance metrics.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide, operate and maintain our digital marketing services and website.</li>
    <li>
      To communicate with you about project updates, campaign performance, invoices and
      support.
    </li>
    <li>
      To send marketing communications, newsletters and promotional offers — you can opt
      out at any time.
    </li>
    <li>
      To analyse website traffic and user behaviour so we can improve the site and our
      services.
    </li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms and service agreements.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Disclosure of your information</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not sell, trade or rent your personal information to third parties.</strong>
    {' '}We may share your data with:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers.</strong> Trusted third-party vendors, hosting providers
      and analytics partners who help us operate our business and website, subject to
      strict confidentiality obligations.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal requirements.</strong> Law enforcement agencies, regulatory bodies or
      authorised third parties where required by law, or to protect the rights, property
      or safety of {site.legalName}, our clients or others.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Data security</h2>
  <p>
    We implement appropriate technical, administrative and physical security measures
    designed to protect your personal information from unauthorised access, alteration,
    disclosure or destruction. However, no electronic transmission over the internet or
    information storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your data protection rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on your location, you may have the following rights over your data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> — request copies of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Rectification</strong> — request correction of inaccurate or incomplete
      information.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Erasure</strong> — request deletion of your personal data, under certain
      conditions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Object or restrict</strong> — object to or restrict processing of your data
      for marketing or other purposes.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, email us at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>This website uses two third-party measurement tools, which set cookies in your browser:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics</strong> (Google LLC) — to understand how visitors find and use
      the site, such as which pages are viewed and where visits come from.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Meta Pixel</strong> (Meta Platforms, Inc.) — to measure the results of our
      advertising on Facebook and Instagram and to show relevant ads to people who have
      visited the site.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These tools record events such as page views, an enquiry being sent, or a tap on our
    WhatsApp, phone or email links. They do not receive the contents of the enquiry form.
    Google and Meta process this data under their own privacy policies. You can refuse or
    delete cookies in your browser settings, install the
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>,
    and manage ad preferences in your Facebook or Instagram account settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our contact form is processed by our hosting provider, which may log technical request
    data in order to deliver the form submission and filter spam.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Contact</h2>
  <p>For any questions or requests regarding this policy, please contact us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
    <li>Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.phoneIntl}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a></li>
  </ul>
  <address>
    {addressLines.map((line) => <span>{line}</span>)}
  </address>
</Legal>
